// ===========================================================================
// 03 - CLAIMS AND LOSS RISK
//
// STRUCTURAL LIMITATION - read before building any service-level claims visual.
//
// The UPS claims extract carries Sub-Parent, Account, and Claims Category. It
// does NOT carry a product, service, or tracking number. There is therefore no
// join path from Fact_Claims to Dim_ServiceMapping, and no honest way to state
// a loss claim rate "by service".
//
// The build guide assigns 30% of the recommendation score to Loss Claim Rate.
// That weight cannot be allocated from this data. Three options, in order of
// preference:
//
//   A. Request a service or tracking-number field on the claims export.
//      This is the only real fix and is the first item on the automation
//      backlog. Until then:
//   B. Score claims at the ACCOUNT level (fully supported today) and use it
//      to drive account-level action rather than service selection.
//   C. If leadership insists on a service-level figure, present the allocated
//      proxy below with its assumption stated on the visual, and never let it
//      drive the headline recommendation.
//
// Measures in this file are grouped by which of those three tiers they belong
// to, and the proxy measures carry the word "Proxy" in their names so they
// cannot be mistaken for measured fact on a report page.
// ===========================================================================

// --- Tier B: supported claim measures (account grain) ----------------------

Issued Claims Pkgs =
SUM ( Fact_Claims[IssuedClaimsPkgQty] )

Paid Claims Pkgs =
SUM ( Fact_Claims[PaidClaimsPkgQty] )

Registered Claims Pkgs =
SUM ( Fact_Claims[RegisteredClaimsPkgQty] )

Paid Claims Amount =
SUM ( Fact_Claims[PaidClaimsAmount] )

Claims Declared Value =
SUM ( Fact_Claims[ClaimsDeclaredValue] )

Loss Claims =
CALCULATE (
    [Issued Claims Pkgs],
    KEEPFILTERS ( Fact_Claims[ClaimsCategory] = "Loss" )
)

Damage Claims =
CALCULATE (
    [Issued Claims Pkgs],
    KEEPFILTERS ( Fact_Claims[ClaimsCategory] = "Damage" )
)

Loss Claims Paid Amount =
CALCULATE (
    [Paid Claims Amount],
    KEEPFILTERS ( Fact_Claims[ClaimsCategory] = "Loss" )
)

// Recovery rate on submitted claims. A low rate is a claims-process problem,
// not a carrier-reliability problem, and belongs in a different conversation.
Claims Recovery Rate =
DIVIDE ( [Paid Claims Pkgs], [Issued Claims Pkgs] )

Avg Paid per Claim =
DIVIDE ( [Paid Claims Amount], [Paid Claims Pkgs] )

// Claims are rare events. Expressed as a bare percentage they render as
// "0.05%" and every service looks identical. Per 10,000 shipments is the
// readable unit and is what belongs on an executive card.
Loss Claim Rate per 10k =
DIVIDE ( [Loss Claims], [Rankable Shipments] ) * 10000

Claims Rate per 10k =
DIVIDE ( [Issued Claims Pkgs], [Rankable Shipments] ) * 10000

// Retained for continuity with the original build guide's KPI list.
Loss Claim Rate =
DIVIDE ( [Loss Claims], [Rankable Shipments] )

Exception / Claims Rate =
DIVIDE ( [Issued Claims Pkgs], [Rankable Shipments] )

// Financial exposure per 1,000 shipments - the version of claims risk a CFO
// reacts to.
Claims Cost per 1k Shipments =
DIVIDE ( [Paid Claims Amount], [Rankable Shipments] ) * 1000


// --- Concentration ---------------------------------------------------------
//
// The single most useful thing this data says about claims is not the firm-wide
// rate; it is how unevenly that rate is distributed across accounts. These
// measures quantify the concentration so it can be stated as a number rather
// than eyeballed off a bar chart.

Firm-wide Loss Rate per 10k =
CALCULATE (
    [Loss Claim Rate per 10k],
    REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_Account, Dim_ServiceMapping )
)

// How many times the firm average this account's loss rate runs. Anything
// above ~2.0x on meaningful volume is an account-level intervention.
Loss Rate Index vs Firm =
DIVIDE ( [Loss Claim Rate per 10k], [Firm-wide Loss Rate per 10k] )

Loss Risk Flag =
VAR Idx = [Loss Rate Index vs Firm]
VAR Vol = [Rankable Shipments]
RETURN
    SWITCH (
        TRUE (),
        ISBLANK ( [Loss Claims] ) || [Loss Claims] = 0, "No loss activity",
        Vol < 500, "Insufficient volume to rate",
        Idx >= 3, "Critical - investigate",
        Idx >= 2, "Elevated - monitor",
        Idx >= 1, "Above firm average",
        "At or below firm average"
    )

// Share of all loss claims sitting in the highest-concentration account.
// Answers "is this a UPS problem or an account problem?" in one number.
Top Account Share of Loss Claims =
VAR ByAccount =
    ADDCOLUMNS (
        CALCULATETABLE ( VALUES ( Dim_Account[AccountKey] ), REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_Account ) ),
        "@Loss", [Loss Claims]
    )
VAR TotalLoss = SUMX ( ByAccount, [@Loss] )
VAR TopLoss = MAXX ( ByAccount, [@Loss] )
RETURN
    DIVIDE ( TopLoss, TotalLoss )

Top Account by Loss Claims =
VAR ByAccount =
    ADDCOLUMNS (
        CALCULATETABLE ( VALUES ( Dim_Account[AccountName] ), REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_Account ) ),
        "@Loss", [Loss Claims]
    )
RETURN
    CONCATENATEX ( TOPN ( 1, ByAccount, [@Loss], DESC ), Dim_Account[AccountName] )


// --- Tier C: allocated service proxy - handle with care --------------------
//
// Distributes account-level loss claims across the service groups that account
// actually shipped on, in proportion to shipment volume. The assumption is
// explicit and almost certainly wrong in detail: it presumes loss risk is
// uniform across services within an account, which is precisely the hypothesis
// the metric would be used to test. It is circular, and it is offered only so
// that a leadership request for a service view can be met with a labelled
// estimate instead of a refusal or - far worse - an unlabelled guess.
//
// Never place these on the Executive Overview or the Annual Recommendation
// page. Data Quality page and analyst drillthrough only.

Loss Claims (Allocated Proxy) =
SUMX (
    VALUES ( Dim_Account[AccountKey] ),
    VAR AccountLoss = CALCULATE ( [Loss Claims], REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_ServiceMapping ) )
    VAR AccountVolumeAllServices =
        CALCULATE ( [Rankable Shipments], REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_ServiceMapping ) )
    VAR VolumeInScope = [Rankable Shipments]
    RETURN
        AccountLoss * DIVIDE ( VolumeInScope, AccountVolumeAllServices )
)

Loss Claim Rate per 10k (Allocated Proxy) =
DIVIDE ( [Loss Claims (Allocated Proxy)], [Rankable Shipments] ) * 10000

Claims Attribution Warning =
"Allocated estimate. The claims extract carries no service or tracking key; "
    & "account-level claims are distributed across services by shipment volume. "
    & "Not a measured service-level loss rate. Do not use for service selection."
